  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the technical capacity of the Pacific small island developing States (SIDS) for sustainable smart mobility in response to climate change issues</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Island nations are highly vulnerable to climate change impacts, such as rising sea levels and flooding, while lacking the technological capacity and infrastructure for effective smart mobility solutions. These challenges, along with increased traffic congestion and socioeconomic losses, highlight the urgent need for the transfer of smart mobility technologies.  The goal is to transfer Korea&apos;s advanced smart mobility technologies to these countries, contributing to poverty reduction, improved quality of life, and climate change mitigation through reduced carbon emissions in the transport sector.  Through UN ESCAP, the project will develop a smart mobility master plan, pilot an ITS and real-time flood monitoring system in urban areas, and provide capacity-building programs for local officials to manage these systems effectively.</narrative>
  </description>
